<section #sh-subject | `<subject>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *subject*. Compiles to eHTML `<subject>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<subject>`

<code-block #code:sh-subject-1>
<meta>
  <subject | Ecology of large mammals>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-subject-1>
<meta>
  <subject | Ecology of large mammals>
</meta>
</minipage>

*Free-form subject. Common for general-interest documents.*

<code-block #code:sh-subject-2>
<meta>
  <subject scheme=MSC2020 | 92D40>
  <subject scheme=MSC2020 | 92D25>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-subject-2>
<meta>
  <subject scheme=MSC2020 | 92D40>
  <subject scheme=MSC2020 | 92D25>
</meta>
</minipage>

*Multiple subjects from a controlled vocabulary. The scheme
identifies the classification system; the JATS exporter
generates the appropriate &lt;subj-group subj-group-type="..."&gt; wrapper.*

<sub-section | Arguments>

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `scheme` | kwarg |  | Optional classification scheme this subject belongs to (e.g. |

<section #sh-subtitle | `<subtitle>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *subtitle*. Compiles to eHTML `<subtitle>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<subtitle>`

<code-block #code:sh-subtitle-1>
<meta>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
  <subtitle | A Multi-Year Field Study in Tanzania>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-subtitle-1>
<meta>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
  <subtitle | A Multi-Year Field Study in Tanzania>
</meta>
</minipage>

<section #sh-title | `<title>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *title*. Compiles to eHTML `<title>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<title>`

<code-block #code:sh-title-1>
<meta>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-title-1>
<meta>
  <title | The Effect of Elephants on Climate>
</meta>
</minipage>

*Inside &lt;article&gt;, &lt;title&gt; in &lt;meta&gt; becomes &lt;article-title&gt;.*

<code-block #code:sh-title-2>
<book>
  <meta>
    <title | A Comprehensive Guide>
  </meta>
</book>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-title-2>
<book>
  <meta>
    <title | A Comprehensive Guide>
  </meta>
</book>
</minipage>

*Inside &lt;book&gt;, &lt;title&gt; in &lt;meta&gt; becomes &lt;book-title&gt;.*

<code-block #code:sh-title-3>
<meta>
  <title | The role of <i type=taxonomic | Loxodonta africana> in ecosystem dynamics>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-title-3>
<meta>
  <title | The role of <i type=taxonomic | Loxodonta africana> in ecosystem dynamics>
</meta>
</minipage>

*Titles can contain inline elements. The recursive content parsing
handles nested constructs.*

<section #sh-version | `<version>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *version*. Compiles to eHTML `<version>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<version>`

<code-block #code:sh-version-1>
<meta>
  <version | 1.0.0>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-version-1>
<meta>
  <version | 1.0.0>
</meta>
</minipage>

*Semantic version. Other formats are equally valid as a free-form
string.*

<code #code:sh-version-2>
<meta version="draft-2" />
</code>

<minipage #mp:sh-version-2>
<meta version="draft-2" />
</minipage>

*Kwarg-form authoring lifts to the child-tag form at the gate.*
